      <sectiondef kind="user-defined">
      <header>Configuration lookup function</header>
      <description><para>Provides the function for configuration lookup, in <ref refid="xiicps__sinit_8c" kindref="compound">xiicps_sinit.c</ref>. </para></description>
      <memberdef kind="function" id="group__iicps__api_1gafaf109c7bf0040c29f861d439bd6613f" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type><ref refid="struct_x_iic_ps___config" kindref="compound">XIicPs_Config</ref> *</type>
        <definition>XIicPs_Config * XIicPs_LookupConfig</definition>
        <argsstring>(UINTPTR BaseAddress)</argsstring>
        <name>XIicPs_LookupConfig</name>
        <param>
          <type>UINTPTR</type>
          <declname>BaseAddress</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Looks up the device configuration by device ID or base address. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Looks up the device configuration based on the unique device ID/BaseAddress. The XIicPs_ConfigTable[] contains the configuration info for each device in the system.</para><para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">BaseAddress</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Contains the base address of the device.</para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>A pointer to the configuration found or NULL if the specified device ID/BaseAddress was not found. See <ref refid="xiicps_8h" kindref="compound">xiicps.h</ref> for the definition of <ref refid="struct_x_iic_ps___config" kindref="compound">XIicPs_Config</ref>.</para></simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>In XSCT/classic flow, DeviceId is used to look up the device configuration. </para></simplesect>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
